WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:03.650
Speaker 1: This next story is absolutely fascinating.

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:06.490
Many of you might remember the name Sidney
Powell.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:13.940
Sidney Powell is this kooky lawyer who was,
you know, she was working with Trump on the

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.530
election fraud claims.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.859
And then when she got to cartoonish, she was
no longer working with Trump, per the White

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:20.859
House.

00:00:20.859 --> 00:00:26.449
But then she was seen at the White House,
and she filed a bunch of these bogus court

00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:29.710
legal complaints, all of which were thrown
out.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:30.710
She is now admitting.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:35.690
Maybe all that stuff she was saying about
the election was not true.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.559
Now I think we really have to approach this
with a skeptical eye, maybe even a cynical

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:41.879
perspective.

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:48.679
Has she really changed her mind or is she
saying this because she is now in such jeopardy

00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:50.440
because of the things that she did?

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:56.460
There's a very interesting vice news article
titled Sidney Powell finally admits that perhaps

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:04.159
the Kraken is not real, but it also says facing
disbarment and several billion dollar lawsuits,

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:10.210
the pro-Trump lawyer is kind of changing her
story, and I think we have to consider the

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.860
context here.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:16.980
The admission from Powell came in a brief
filed Monday to the U.S. Court of Appeal for

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.490
the Sixth District.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:24.110
It was signed by Powell and fellow lawyer
Howard Klein, handler filed on behalf of several

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:31.869
other Kraken lawyers, though notably not pro-Trump
lawyer Lin Wood, who's also a party back in

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:32.869
August.

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:35.900
You might remember and we covered this at
the time, District Court Judge Linda Parker

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:42.640
eviscerated Powell and her team, saying the
lawsuit represents a historic and profound

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.689
abuse of the judicial process.

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:45.969
And it does.

00:01:45.969 --> 00:01:50.439
It's one thing to take on the charge of vindicating
rights associated with an allegedly fraudulent

00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:51.439
election.

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:56.020
It is another to take on the charge of deceiving
a federal court and the American people into

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:00.470
believing rights were infringed without regard
to whether any laws or rights were in fact

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.679
violated.

00:02:01.679 --> 00:02:03.670
And that is what happened here.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:06.880
Now, Powell, this is fascinating.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.770
Powell has argued at the time she was under
no obligation to thoroughly research the claims

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:16.050
that she made about voter fraud in the lawsuit.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.240
She sort of made the case at the time.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:23.700
Listen, people came to me and they said, this
is what happened, and it's not up to me to

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.490
independently verify that that's what the
case is.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:31.390
I'm just the lawyer here, which the judge
does not agree with, and it makes absolutely

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.690
no sense.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:40.250
In this week's filing, Powell and Klein handler
casually admit everything they had been saying

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:46.141
may not actually be true, but because lots
of people were saying it at the time, they

00:02:46.141 --> 00:02:48.510
decided to include it.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:54.320
Quote Millions of Americans believe the central
contentions of the complaint to be true, and

00:02:54.320 --> 00:03:02.980
perhaps they are admitting she's no longer
actually confident about the veracity of those

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:03.980
claims.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:09.950
Now, I think it's important to ask the question
Does she believe all of these wacky election

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.410
claims are true?

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:15.600
But she's backing off because of the legal
problems that she's now happening?

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.230
She's now having.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:21.870
Did she never believe the claims were true
or did she believe them, and she has since

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.900
changed her mind?

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:26.800
Legally speaking, I don't know that it makes
a difference.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.590
As a reminder, here are some of the wacky
things that this woman said.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:36.730
Speaker 2: The amount of evidence that this
election was completely fraudulent and that

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:40.250
Joe Biden is a fraudulent president is beyond
overwhelming.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:46.320
Speaker 1: Now, understand that if we are
to believe her current statement, what she

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:52.220
meant when she said that was the people I'm
working with told me this, but I don't really

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.510
know it to be true.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.520
That's what she now says.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.120
Listen, we were told these things.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.070
We didn't independently confirm them.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.480
Here's another Sidney Powell clip.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:03.810
Speaker 3: So I don't know where to go next,
because this is like something out of a movie.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:06.960
So the Department of Defense, let's review.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:07.960
Yeah.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:12.510
2006 a pattern coming from the Department
of Defense that allows for an algorithm that

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.590
can flip and change votes.

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:18.729
The patent was transferred to
Speaker 1: I love the reference to an algorithm.

00:04:18.729 --> 00:04:20.530
Now it's an algorithm.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:26.729
Speaker 2: It can predetermine that algorithm
can predetermine the outcome of an election

00:04:26.729 --> 00:04:30.219
and specifically to.

00:04:30.219 --> 00:04:31.900
Create a predetermined outcome.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:37.169
Speaker 1: OK, so maybe she believed that
to be true at the time or again, maybe that's

00:04:37.169 --> 00:04:41.439
just what some of the people she was working
with told her.

00:04:41.439 --> 00:04:43.000
Here's another one about a secret server.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:49.230
Speaker 2: What I think really has to be discovered
is that there is a secret server that all

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.599
the votes go to where they manipulate the
heck out of it.

00:04:52.599 --> 00:04:56.639
Speaker 1: Now, did she believe that at the
time, or was that also just something people

00:04:56.639 --> 00:04:57.639
were telling her?

00:04:57.639 --> 00:05:00.900
And here's one last one with this wacky guy,
Stu Peters,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:07.650
Speaker 2: that for at least 20 years now,
somebody other than the voters of the United

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:14.490
States of America has been determining certain
elections, and this year, if not prior years,

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:17.639
it happened to be the presidency of the United
States of America.

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:23.720
Speaker 1: Now, did she believe that at the
time or again, was it just we were told that

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.729
stuff and we didn't investigate it.

00:05:25.729 --> 00:05:29.720
So Sidney Powell now saying we don't really
know that any of that stuff was true.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.720
It's just what we were told, just what we
were told by plaintiffs.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.610
She's really potentially in trouble here,
and I think that's all that's going on.

